    "result_text": "Everything is green. The full test suite (the `AcceptanceTest`, which is the only test class in the project) passes, and the whole project compiles.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required: when a new owner isn't a hard duplicate but shares an existing owner's `lastName` and `postcode` with a *different* telephone, still create it and return `possibleDuplicate: true` with `possibleDuplicateOf` set to the matching owner's id (otherwise `possibleDuplicate: false`). The flags are read back via `GET /api/owners/{id}`, so they must be persisted.\n\nI kept structural impact low by adding behaviour as small, cohesive units rather than growing the large `OwnerRestControllerV1` or `Owner` classes:\n\n1. **New helper `PossibleDuplicates.java`** \u2014 a small self-contained class (mirroring the existing `Namesakes`/`CityCodes`/`Identities` pattern) whose `matchId(...)` returns the soft-matching owner's id or `null`. All the new logic lives here, in a class with essentially zero surrounding complexity.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 a single added line: `owner.setPossibleDuplicateOf(PossibleDuplicates.matchId(owners, owner));`, placed alongside the existing `setNamesakeCount`/`setBulkSignupWarning` calls. This is the only existing method I edited (1 changed line, CC unchanged).\n\n3. **`Owner.java`** \u2014 one persisted field `possibleDuplicateOf` plus trivial getter/setter and a derived `getPossibleDuplicate()` (returns `possibleDuplicateOf != null`), so only one column is stored and the boolean is derived. Each new method is CC=1.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the two `readOnly` fields to the `Owner` schema so the generated `OwnerDto` carries them; MapStruct auto-maps them from the matching `Owner` getters (no mapper change needed).\n\n5. **DB schema/data (hsqldb)** \u2014 added the `possible_duplicate_of INTEGER` column and updated the positional seed inserts to match.",
